  "reason": "Evidence: config_008 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat, acc=0.7207) is the clear best, showing that the ViT-L image encoder and transformer aggregation are strongly beneficial over resnet50/avgpool. The only untested variable within this top-performing sub-space is the fusion strategy (weighted vs concat). Question: Does weighted fusion improve over simple concatenation when combining the two modalities with the best-performing encoders and aggregation? This is a clean single-variable extension of the current best result, isolating the fusion effect. It is the best next experiment because it directly exploits the strongest evidence (ViT-L + transformer) at minimal additional cost (~4.7 GPU hours, comparable to config_008's 4.65), and the result will tell us whether to lock in concat or switch to weighted for all subsequent experiments, reducing uncertainty before we test RNA encoder alternatives (scgpt, pca_n2000) in the remaining budget."
}

